-- ISO-14097-01 user_type  (quote 476 chars)
update public.fields set verification_status='needs_engineer_review', verification_quote='The following table describes the use cases of both direct users of the Standard and potential users of the information provided by organizations in compliance with the standard: | USERS USE CASE Financial Institutions • Set target and identify action for climate contributions to voluntary commitment Climate platforms and track their performance over time Policymakers Report on contribution to climate targets via emerging mandatory reporting programs Financial Authorities — p.3', verification_note='pdf-verified 2026-09-08 (p.3) [VA] - SOURCE IS THE NOV-2017 WG SCOPING DOCUMENT, NOT THE PUBLISHED ISO 14097: descriptive/advisory text, no normative requirement behind this field; the three user rows are printed in the USERS column of the p.3 table; the text layer interleaves that column with the USE CASE column', verified_at=now() where id='bdc37a68-67c6-448e-b491-6e4342eaf806' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- ISO-14097-01 support_function  (quote 567 chars)
update public.fields set verification_status='needs_engineer_review', verification_quote='The standard will support investors’ work on climate-­‐related issues by: 1. Harmonizing definitions, concepts and methodological frameworks related to the measurement of contributions to climate goals (mitigation and adaptation) and exposure to climate-­‐related risks; 2. Identifying relevant climate actions for each type of financial activity; 3. Provide reporting and communication requirements and guidance for financial institutions; and 4. Provide a measurement framework to connect financial activities to their impact on mitigation/adaptation on the ground. — p.3', verification_note='pdf-verified 2026-09-08 (p.3) [VA] - SOURCE IS THE NOV-2017 WG SCOPING DOCUMENT, NOT THE PUBLISHED ISO 14097: descriptive/advisory text, no normative requirement behind this field; closed four-item list; this is what the FUTURE standard is proposed to do, not a requirement on a user', verified_at=now() where id='c40a225b-4c91-40a9-a3e7-15f4bd2e68d1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- ISO-14097-02 climate_objective  (quote 394 chars)
update public.fields set verification_status='needs_engineer_review', verification_quote='our review concludes that financial institutions can fundamentally pursue two climate-­‐related objectives through their investments and lending activities: 1. Managing climate-­‐related financial risks and opportunities, by better assessing, mitigating and hedging them. 2. Contributing to the achievement of climate goals, through the influence they have on investee companies’ GHG emissions. — §3.1, p.39', verification_note='pdf-verified 2026-09-08 (§3.1, p.39) [VA] - SOURCE IS THE NOV-2017 WG SCOPING DOCUMENT, NOT THE PUBLISHED ISO 14097: descriptive/advisory text, no normative requirement behind this field; the enum value "both" rests on p.39 "they very often mix these two objectives: sometimes because they pursue both at the same time"', verified_at=now() where id='2f6ad359-d09d-42ec-97ce-6741d8dabf2a' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- ISO-14097-02 objective_clarified  (quote 574 chars)
update public.fields set verification_status='needs_engineer_review', verification_quote='The review of financial institutions’ narratives related to their climate actions reveals that they very often mix these two objectives: sometimes because they pursue both at the same time, sometimes because they primarily seek reputational benefits, without a clear understanding of the actual concrete outcomes expected. | Clarify the objective(s) addressed by the standard based on the current objectives pursued by financial institutions, these being i.) the management of climate-­‐related financial risks; and ii.) the contribution to the achievement of climate goals. — §3.1, p.39 + Introduction, p.4', verification_note='pdf-verified 2026-09-08 (§3.1, p.39 + Introduction, p.4) [VA] - SOURCE IS THE NOV-2017 WG SCOPING DOCUMENT, NOT THE PUBLISHED ISO 14097: descriptive/advisory text, no normative requirement behind this field; a recommendation addressed to the ISO 14097 working group, not an obligation on a reporting entity', verified_at=now() where id='c53847d8-57ed-4f82-a5e1-759e546002fb' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- ISO-14097-02 kpi_objective_specific  (quote 456 chars)
update public.fields set verification_status='needs_engineer_review', verification_quote='A more consistent process to pursue these objectives, could potentially include: i. the identification of the available climate-­‐related actions (e.g. portfolio construction, engagement) that are consistent with the objective; ii.the definition of KPIs that will allow the for measurement of results of the action; iii. setting a target based on the relevant actions and measuring its progress. This process was however not observed in current disclosure. — §1.3, p.9', verification_note='pdf-verified 2026-09-08 (§1.3, p.9) [VA] - SOURCE IS THE NOV-2017 WG SCOPING DOCUMENT, NOT THE PUBLISHED ISO 14097: descriptive/advisory text, no normative requirement behind this field; the source frames this as what a process "could potentially include", explicitly not as a requirement', verified_at=now() where id='912bc5db-81d6-432c-8358-1b46f22dfd79' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

